{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WHh7DnwEXvej6nFayJQCf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand what needs to be done next.\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations diverge in observable behavior. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies via differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Components: cmd/ (utilities), pkg/sys/ (syscall abstractions), pkg/format/ (formatting), pkg/testutils/ (differential testing harness), magefiles/ (build targets).\n\n**Current State**: \n- Source code exists for: pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/wc\n\n\n- Specs are complete for: pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/wc, cmd/cat, cmd/sponge, cmd/ls, cmd/du\n- Code generation hasn't run on the current branch yet; implementations are tracked at generation-merged tags\n\nLooking at the release status, I can see the progression: rel00.0 covers the foundational packages with specs done but code not started, rel01.0 handles wc, rel01.1 covers cat, and rel01.2 is partially listed.\n\nThe remaining releases show sponge and du in rel01.2 and rel01.3 with specs complete but code not started, while rel02.0 through rel02.2 are still pending specs for utilities like tee, head, true, false, yes, basename, and dirname. The deferred releases rel99.0 through rel99.2 cover ls and ts variants that are spec-complete but intentionally deferred.\n\nThe allowed releases are constrained to rel00.0 through rel02.2, excluding the deferred ones. Looking at what's already in source_code, I see cmd/wc/main.go exists along with the format and sys packages, though the listing appears to be cut off.\n\nThe existing implementation covers testutils fully, sys fully, and format partially with columns and size modules. The wc command is fully implemented. Since rel00.0 is the earliest incomplete release, I need to check what's required there—it has three use cases for magefiles, format, and sys that all have specs complete but no code started yet.\n\nHowever, looking at the actual source code, testutils, sys, and format already have implementations despite the code_status field saying \"not started\"—the source code takes precedence over stale documentation. For magefiles, the design decision excludes them from generation scope since they're provided by cobbler-scaffold, though cmd/version is a valid target since it's explicitly mentioned in the design decision. I'm seeing that cmd/wc already exists in the source code, but several commands are missing—cat, sponge, and du all have complete specs but no implementation yet, while the rel02.0 commands don't even have specs finalized. Since rel00.0's foundational packages are mostly in place, the next logical step is tackling rel01.1 with the cat command implementation. I also need to look at rel01.0 (wc). cmd/wc exists in source_code, but the code_status says \"not started\". Since I trust source_code over prose, cmd/wc is implemented.\n\nBut wait — cmd/wc exists but does it have tests? There's no wc_test.go in the source_code. Let me check... the source_code section only shows cmd/wc/main.go. No test file. So I might need to create differential tests for wc.\n\nActually, looking at the constraints more carefully: \"Do NOT explore the filesystem, read files, or run commands.\" I can only work with what's provided. The source_code shows cmd/wc/main.go but no test file. So wc tests might be needed.\n\nI'm working with limited information here — I have the architecture docs, source code, and code_status inline, but I don't have the actual PRD content for wc, cat, sponge, du, and other tools. I only know they exist. Looking at what's actually done, rel00.0 is mostly complete with pkg/format, pkg/sys, and pkg/testutils all present in source_code. The only potential gap is cmd/version from the magefiles PRD. For rel01.0, I've got cmd/wc but need to verify if tests are required. main.go exists, but no tests visible in source_code. Need wc_test.go with differential tests.\n\nrel01.1 (cat): no code exists. Needs implementation + tests.\n\nI can only propose 1 task (constraint: \"Do NOT exceed 1 tasks\").\n\nPriority order: earliest incomplete release first. rel01.0 is wc — the implementation exists but we might need tests. Or rel01.1 is cat — needs everything.\n\nActually, let me look more carefully at rel00.0. The format package has columns.go, doc.go, and size.go with column alignment and size formatting working, but I don't see ANSI color support implemented. The doc.go mentions it implements prd003-format R1 and R3, so if R2 is the color codes, that's potentially missing — though without the actual PRD I can't confirm what's required.\n\nGiven I can only pick one task, I need to focus on what's clearest and most actionable from what I can see. The wc implementation exists and just needs tests, which is straightforward work. tests\n2. cmd/cat implementation (rel01.1) — needs implementation\n3. cmd/sponge implementation (rel01.2) — needs implementation\n\nFor wc tests, I know the PRD is prd005-wc (from the code comments). The test file would be cmd/wc/wc_test.go. I can reference testutils patterns from the existing code.\n\nFor cat implementation, I'd need the PRD (prd??? for cat) which I don't have inline.\n\nActually, I should focus on what's most clearly defined. Let me look at what tests look like — from the source_code, I have pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go and pkg/sys/*_test.go as examples.\n\nFor cmd/wc, the test file would use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests to compare the Go wc binary against the GNU reference binary. This is the differential testing pattern described in the architecture.\n\nNow I can anchor the wc test task to the specific requirements from prd005-wc. Looking at cmd/wc/main.go, I can extract the key requirements: default behavior outputs lines, words, and bytes; reading from stdin when no files are provided; -m flag taking precedence over -c; tab expansion for max line length calculations; fixed output column ordering; proper output formatting; total line handling; --files0-from support; and locale-aware character counting. These requirements map directly to the test cases I'd need to write.\n\nThe constraint is one task, max 250 lines, max 4 requirements. I should pick the most critical ones to test first. I need to cover the remaining requirements for the differential tests: R2 handles individual and combined flags with precedence rules, R3 validates output formatting across single and multiple files, and R4 tests edge cases like empty files, binary data, and error handling. I'm also considering whether the test file needs to build the wc binary itself, similar to how the example tests do it.\n\nFor the test setup, I'd need to build the Go wc binary in a temporary directory and locate the GNU reference binary, then pass both to the differential test runner. I should also check if there's a test specification document like test-rel-01.0.yaml that defines the exact test cases to reference.\n\nLet me verify this stays within the constraints: one task, around 150-200 lines, one file to create, four requirements tied to the PRD IDs. This looks solid, so I'll write it up now.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39656,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39656},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0dd9c13a-c418-4824-bde5-23b3beb412ae","uuid":"c66a11ad-d661-44a9-8086-0b4c24e324ac"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WHh7DnwEXvej6nFayJQCf8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Components: `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build targets, scaffolded externally).\n\n**Implementation State** (from source_code — trusted over prose):\n- `pkg/testutils` — implemented (difftest.go + tests + testbin helper)\n- `pkg/sys` — implemented (signal, stat, terminal + platform files + tests)\n- `pkg/format` — implemented (columns.go, size.go, doc.go)\n- `cmd/wc` — implemented (main.go, ~410 lines), **no test file present**\n\n**Current Release Priority**: rel00.0 infrastructure is largely done (pkg/ code exists; magefiles excluded by DD7). rel01.0 (wc) has the implementation but is missing its differential test file (`cmd/wc/wc_test.go`). This is the earliest incomplete deliverable.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nrel01.0-uc001-wc is the earliest use case with incomplete work: `cmd/wc/main.go` exists and implements prd005-wc R1–R6, but there is no `wc_test.go` with differential tests against the GNU `gwc` reference binary. Per P5 (dependency ordering), tests follow implementation. Per P8, implementation before tests when split. The wc differential test is the single highest-priority task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"cmd/wc differential tests (prd005-wc R1, R2, R3, R4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (implementation under test -- covers prd005-wc R1 through R6)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests harness)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go (reference pattern for building test binaries in TestMain and structuring differential tests)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd005-wc.yaml (requirements to verify)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-01.0.yaml (test case inventory for this release)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/wc/wc_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go wc against GNU gwc reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Create a TestMain function that builds the Go wc binary from the current\n          package (go build -o <tmpdir>/wc .) and locates the GNU reference binary\n          gwc (Homebrew-installed GNU coreutils). Skip all tests if gwc is not found\n          on PATH. Clean up the built binary after tests complete.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Create differential test cases for default behavior and stdin processing\n          (prd005-wc R1). Test cases must cover: reading from stdin with no flags\n          (default lines + words + bytes), reading from one named file, reading from\n          multiple named files with total line, and \"-\" as explicit stdin argument.\n          Use pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests with the Go binary and gwc reference binary.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Create differential test cases for flag behavior (prd005-wc R2, R5). Test\n          cases must cover: individual flags -l, -w, -c, -m, -L; combined short\n          flags -lwc; -m precedence over -c when both given (R2.3); long flag forms\n          --lines, --words, --bytes, --chars, --max-line-length; and tab expansion\n          for -L (R2.5). All tests run under LC_ALL=C (R5.2).\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Create differential test cases for output formatting and edge cases\n          (prd005-wc R3, R4, R6). Test cases must cover: --total=always,\n          --total=never, --total=only modes (R3.3); empty file input; file with no\n          trailing newline; nonexistent file producing error on stderr with exit\n          code 1 (R6.1); and column width alignment matching GNU output (R2.6).\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Follow the TestMain binary-build pattern from pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go:\n          build the Go binary once in TestMain, store the path in a package-level\n          variable, and clean up with os.RemoveAll after m.Run().\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Locate the GNU reference binary using exec.LookPath(\"gwc\"). If gwc is not\n          found, print a skip message and exit 0 from TestMain so that tests are\n          skipped gracefully in environments without Homebrew GNU coreutils.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          All DiffTest entries must set LC_ALL=C in their Env field (or rely on\n          the default LC_ALL=C from pkg/testutils.buildEnv) per architecture\n          design decision DD6.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/wc/wc_test.go compiles with no errors (go vet ./cmd/wc/...).\n      - id: AC2\n        text: |\n          When gwc is available on PATH, go test ./cmd/wc/ runs all differential\n          tests and they pass -- stdout, stderr, and exit code match between the\n          Go binary and gwc for every test case.\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          When gwc is not available on PATH, go test ./cmd/wc/ skips gracefully\n          with no failures.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: |\n          At least 15 DiffTest entries are defined, covering the requirement areas\n          in R2, R3, and R4 (default behavior, flag combinations, output formatting,\n          edge cases).\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39656,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39656},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0dd9c13a-c418-4824-bde5-23b3beb412ae","uuid":"9ae9b5ba-f38d-4990-a41a-8716db066ead"}
